# Reviewed exceptions, not a blanket suppression. Each entry names the finding,
# why it does not apply to this static site, and what change removes it.
# Review by 2027-04-01.
#
# S3 encryption without a customer-managed KMS key (terraform/main.tf, site
# bucket). The bucket holds only the public static export, is private behind
# CloudFront Origin Access Control and uses SSE-S3 (AES256). A CMK adds about
# $1/month plus a CloudFront grant in the key policy, with no confidentiality
# gain for pages that are public by design.
AVD-AWS-0132
# CloudFront minimum TLS version (terraform/cloudfront.tf). The site uses the
# default *.cloudfront.net certificate, for which CloudFront fixes the security
# policy; minimum_protocol_version can be set only with a custom ACM
# certificate. Remove this entry with the custom-domain change.
AVD-AWS-0013
